WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.980
Welcome to Planet Orion Daily, episode 96, coming to you on June 20th, 2026.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.200
Here's what's new in science, health, and longevity research.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:18.400
Prion proteins may hide short peptides that kill drug-resistant bacteria, AI analysis shows.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:25.020
University of Pennsylvania scientists used AI to scan Prion and Prion-like sequences,

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:31.700
and identified short Prion in peptides with antibacterial activity against resistant strains.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:37.380
The peptides appear embedded within proteins best known for causing neurodegeneration.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:44.480
Structural modeling suggests the antimicrobial segments are normally masked until proteolytic release.

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.700
Follow-up work will test efficacy and safety in animal infection models.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:56.300
The planetary in spotlight looks at how this AI scanning of Prion sequences uncovered short

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:01.880
embedded peptides with direct antibacterial activity against resistant strains.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:09.320
The finding reframes Prion as potential reservoirs of innate defense molecules rather than solely

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:15.980
pathogenic entities. It opens a route to mind neurodegeneration linked proteins for new antibiotic

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:23.520
scaffolds. Next, researchers will synthesize and test the most promising Prionins in live infection

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.480
models, which other protein families might hide similar overlooked functions.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:37.080
Now, shifting to a very different area of research. A review in nature reviews endocrinology outlines

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:44.280
how Epstein-Barr virus already linked to higher multiple sclerosis risk. Appears to confer protection

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:51.180
against autoimmune type 1 diabetes. The opposite directional effect on two autoimmune conditions

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:54.980
points to a virus-specific modulation of immune tolerance.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:01.960
Researchers note the established multiple sclerosis association provides a useful comparator

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:07.760
for dissecting mechanisms. Further human cohort studies are needed to confirm the protective

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:14.180
association and identify involved pathways. Now, here's something most people get wrong.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:20.460
You've probably heard that hormones such as cytokinins regulate growth only in plants.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:27.960
In reality, the same molecules are now detected in mammalian cells and appear to influence stress

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:34.560
signaling and metabolism. Right now, as your cells manage daily oxidative and nutrient stress,

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:41.080
trace cytokinins from diet or resident microbes may be modulating the same pathways plants

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:47.900
used to slow aging under drought. A single cytokine in molecule can alter gene expression across

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:53.340
dozens of targets, illustrating how a small concentration produces outsized effects.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:03:00.180
The next time you drink green tea or eat certain vegetables, consider that you are also ingesting

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:06.320
compounds once thought are relevant to human biology. Watch for upcoming studies that measure

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:12.560
cytokinine levels in human blood and link them to measurable changes in inflammatory markers.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:18.240
On a different note, Caltech researchers showed that stressed soil bacteria,

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:24.860
remodeled gene expression and metabolism to cope with phosphorus scarcity, altering interactions

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:30.920
with plant roots. The changes affect nutrient cycling and plant growth under nutrient limited

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:38.080
conditions. Experiments combined controlled microcosms with transcriptomic profiling of bacterial

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:44.120
communities. The findings matter for predicting soil responses to changing climate and fertilizer

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:51.960
use. Next up, a fria-universitat Berlin analysis emphasizes that fungal networks move carbon

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:59.520
through soil food webs and stabilize plant communities under stress. Mycorrhizile and sapetrophic

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:05.740
guilds together influence both agricultural yields and long-term carbon sequestration.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:11.080
The review synthesizes field and laboratory evidence across ecosystems.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:17.840
Future work will quantify how management practices alter fungal contributions to soil carbon.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.760
From below ground fungal networks to root associated microbes that specifically aid heat tolerance

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:32.380
in crops. Rhizosphere microbiome surveys suggest certain bacterial and fungal taxa correlate

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:38.500
with improved crop performance under elevated temperatures. Inoculation trials are testing whether

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:44.920
selected consortia can be transplanted to boost resilience. The work focuses on microbes that

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:51.040
influence water uptake and hormone signaling in roots. Field validation across multiple

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:57.700
growing seasons is underway. From beneficial microbes and agriculture to an animal virus that

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:05.620
revealed unexpected tissue preferences during spillover. Early US cattle infections with H5 and 1

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:12.240
produced severe utter disease while largely sparing the respiratory tract, delaying recognition

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:18.840
that the virus had jumped species. Diagnostic sampling focused on milk rather than nasal swabs

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:25.180
proved more sensitive. The altered tissue tropism differs from pattern seen in other mammals.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:30.100
Surveillance programs have since adjusted sampling protocols accordingly.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:37.100
From emerging pathogen behavior to engineered nanobubbles that address environmental contaminants.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:44.980
Nanobubbles roughly 100 nanometers across generate reactive species that break down oil, algae,

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:52.080
and other contaminants without leaving chemical residues. When Zang's team at New Jersey Institute of

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:58.820
Technology is testing the approach in field-scale water treatment systems, the bubbles remain suspended

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:03.700
for long periods and deliver oxidative power directly at pollutant interfaces.

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:09.920
Next steps include scaling generation methods for municipal and agricultural use.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:16.700
University of Copenhagen economist tracked Danish firms facing low-cost Chinese imports.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:23.780
They found that while offshoring reduced local emissions, overall global emissions increased.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:30.140
The net rise occurred because production shifted to regions with higher carbon intensity per unit

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:35.280
output. The study used firm-level data matched to trade and emissions records.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:40.960
Policy makers are examining whether carbon border adjustments could alter this pattern.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:47.620
An international team from Tehoku University, Tokyo University of Science, Vanderbilt,

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:53.900
and Adelaide developed an ambient air method. They used it to synthesize stable 15-atom

00:06:53.900 --> 00:07:00.060
Aridium nanoclusters. The clusters delivered 1.5 times the mass activity of standard

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:04.960
Aridium catalysts. The clusters ran without degradation beyond 20 hours.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:10.260
Precise-size control was achieved without high temperature or vacuum equipment.

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:15.020
Researchers aimed to extend the approach to other precious metal catalysts.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:23.600
JWST observations led by IPCAC at Caltech revealed a massive galaxy cluster.

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:29.960
The cluster acts as a strong gravitational lens at a redshift where such structures were not

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:36.560
expected to be fully assembled. Three papers detailed the cluster's concentration and lensing strength.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:41.420
The data challenge current models of structure formation during cosmic noon.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:48.540
Additional JWST pointings are planned to map member galaxies and dark matter distribution.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:55.760
Researchers generated a high-resolution atlas of the inflorescence meristem in Arabisox,

00:07:56.560 --> 00:08:02.360
identifying 18 transcriptionally distinct cell populations that give rise to stems and flowers.

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:09.120
Single-cell RNA sequencing traced lineage trajectories from stem cell niches outward.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:15.220
The map clarifies how positional information is translated into organ identity.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:21.460
The data set will serve as a reference for crop species with similar meristem organization.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:29.200
University of Technology Sydney physicists demonstrated that rotating atomically thin hexagonal

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:34.900
boron nitride flakes lets them tune the emission properties of embedded quantum emitters.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:39.480
The twist angle alters local strain and dielectric environment,

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:46.240
shifting photon energy and coherence. Experiments combine optical spectroscopy with precise

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:53.000
mechanical rotation stages. The method offers a route to integretable quantum light sources for

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:59.460
photonic circuits. Psychological experiments link heavy platform used to weaken sense of body

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:05.560
ownership, with participants reporting reduced alignment between visual appearance and felt bodily

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:12.700
self. The effect appears tied to repeated exposure to edited images rather than simple screen time.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:20.080
Researchers measured proprioceptive drift and explicit ownership ratings after controlled viewing

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:28.780
sessions. Longitudinal studies are planned to assess reversibility. A survey of 463 German adults

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:36.340
found that familiarity with plants and birds typical of agricultural landscapes drops sharply in younger

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:43.820
cohorts compared with older respondents. Common species such as dandelions remain widely recognized,

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:51.220
while meadow specialists do not. The pattern points to reduce direct contact with farmland biodiversity.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:57.460
Educational programs targeting regional species identification are being developed.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:04.100
New findings continue to show how basic biology and environmental interactions shape health

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:10.920
in measurable ways. Keep an eye on the animal infection model results for the synthesized preon

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:17.920
and peptides. That's Planetarean daily for today. If you enjoyed this, a rating or review on Apple

